tt-local-generator (0.99.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(create): live AnimateDiff previews actually reach the panel. Both stdout
    drains in the animatediff generator forward only lines matching a keyword
    allow-list ("Frame", "Step", "Loading", "Error", ...); a
    "PREVIEW: <step>/<total> <path>" line matches none of them, so every preview
    was written to the run log and then dropped. The runner emitted correctly
    and the panel rendered correctly, but nothing connected them - the feature
    was inert end to end.
  * feat(status bar): the Video indicator now lights while AnimateDiff is
    generating. AnimateDiff is a local subprocess with no managed server, so
    ModelStatusService correctly reports Video as off for the whole run - true,
    but misleading when a video is visibly being made. It lights in the same
    success green as a ready server but with its own glyph, and a tooltip
    naming what is running: a filled dot means "a server is up and can take
    work", and here there is no server at all.

