tt-local-generator (0.97.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(create): the macOS inline-player path now checks `GstPlayer.load()`'s
    return value, not just `.available`. `.available` reports only that
    gtk4paintablesink was created; `load()` fails independently when playbin
    can't be made — so a failed load still returned a widget, turning the
    poster fallback that branch exists to preserve into a blank frame. The
    failed player is now closed and the poster shown. The GstPlayer widget is
    also height-capped to match the Gtk.Video path, so an odd aspect ratio
    can't push the recents strip off-screen. (Copilot PR#26 review.)
  * fix(status bar): a locally painted launch failure now survives the next
    poll. `update_segments()` applied the snapshot unconditionally, so the
    ERROR from a start script we watched exit non-zero was erased on the very
    next tick, hiding the failure tooltip. It now sticks until the segment is
    genuinely READY or the user starts it again. (Copilot PR#26 review.)
  * fix(status bar): a start script exiting non-zero now clears the service's
    starting bookkeeping. `_resolve` reports STARTING while `starting_at` is
    set and within `start_timeout` (180 s), so a failed launch showed a ticking
    "starting" clock for three minutes — and that stale STARTING is precisely
    what overwrote the failure above. (Copilot PR#26 review.)

