tt-local-generator (0.97.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(status bar): the Art LLM indicator no longer lights up because the
    prompt-gen model is running. `artgen.detect_artgen_endpoint()` deliberately
    falls back to the tiny Qwen3-0.6B prompt server on :8001 as a last resort
    (so Inspire keeps working with nothing else up), which makes
    `running_artgen_model()` non-None whenever the auto-started prompt server is
    alive — and v0.97.0 carried the old aggregate's "detected model => artgen is
    ready" override across verbatim, so Art LLM lit off the PROMPT model. That
    is the same "it's just the prompt gen being ready" report the by-function
    bar exists to fix, one layer up. A detection now counts for Art LLM only
    when it isn't a model another segment already owns
    (`status_segments.detected_model_is_artgen`), which also covers the case
    where the prompt server reports an id we don't recognise (matched_key None)
    by checking its port. A genuinely foreign chat model still lights it.
  * fix(status bar): the capability popover's "Generative art" row had the same
    pre-existing flaw, claiming "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B (detected)". Both surfaces are
    now painted from ONE decision so they cannot disagree.

