tt-local-generator (0.97.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * feat(status bar): the bottom bar now shows one indicator per FUNCTION —
    "Prompt · Image · Video · Art LLM" — instead of a single aggregate dot.
    Each carries its own state as a shape as well as a colour (● ready /
    ◐ starting / ○ off / ✕ failed), with the model name and startup phase in
    its tooltip and the existing capability popover unchanged behind a click.
  * fix(status bar): the aggregate dot it replaces folded every server into one
    READY > STARTING > ERROR > OFF state. Since the CPU-only prompt-server is
    auto-started on launch and goes ready within seconds, the bar reported
    "ready" for the entire session no matter what the media servers were doing,
    and the next poll stomped the elapsed timer of any launch in flight — so a
    server start appeared to stop updating partway through. Segments resolve
    independently, so no function can speak for another one.
  * fix(model status): an open port that a DIFFERENT, healthy server is already
    answering on is no longer read as "this server is launching". Every media
    model shares the one port-8000 container (artgen models share 8002), so
    while Wan2.2 was healthy the Image key's probe found :8000 open, its own
    health check failed, and the service inferred STARTING for it forever. The
    old aggregate dot hid this; a per-function bar rendered it as "Image
    starting... 4:32" while nothing was starting. A launch we actually started
    is tracked separately, so genuine starts are unaffected.
  * fix(create): a generated video now PLAYS in the result panel it was made
    in. That branch rendered a static poster thumbnail — an unfinished v1
    placeholder from before the panel was wired into Create — so an .mp4 sat
    still in Create while the Library played it fine. It now builds a real
    player (Gtk.Video with autoplay+loop, GstPlayer on macOS), torn down on
    every state change so a swapped result never leaves a pipeline decoding
    behind the new one.

