tt-local-generator (0.96.4) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(postinst): weight downloads no longer fail with permission errors on a
    box without Docker. STEP 2 created /opt/tenstorrent/models/hub as root:root
    when the 'docker' group is absent, but the tt-model-* postinsts download as
    $SUDO_USER (a non-root user) and download_model.sh prefers that path when it
    exists — so on a fresh install the download failed to write there, silently
    (the download is fail-soft). Now the shared storage falls back to the
    installing user's primary group (not root) when Docker isn't present, so the
    setgid+group-writable dir is actually writable by that user. Container-
    verified: real weights land in /opt/tenstorrent/models/hub as the non-root
    user. (Copilot PR#25 review.)

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Tue, 25 Aug 2026 00:30:00 +0000

tt-local-generator (0.96.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(postinst): `sudo apt install tt-local-generator` from the PPA no longer
    fails to configure on a box without Docker. STEP 3 ran `usermod -aG docker
    $USER` unconditionally; when Docker is not installed the `docker` group does
    not exist, so usermod exited 6 and — under `set -e` — aborted the whole
    postinst (package left half-configured, dependent tt-model-* packages
    blocked). Now it only adds the user when the group exists, defers with clear
    guidance otherwise, and is fail-soft regardless. Container-verified: main +
    tt-model-animatediff now configure cleanly with no docker group present.
  * fix(postinst): correct the misleading checklist note that said tt-installer
    provides "Qwen3 prompt-server GPU support" — the Qwen3-0.6B prompt-server
    runs on CPU; tt-installer provides the tt-metal runtime and the
    torch/transformers the prompt tier uses, not GPU support.
  * docs(README): add "Install from the Tenstorrent PPA (recommended)" — apt
    key + source, `apt install tt-local-generator`, the tt-model-* weight
    packages, and the tt-installer / Docker prerequisites; relabel the
    git-clone flow as "From source (development)".

