tt-local-generator (0.91.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * revert(create): default AnimateDiff multi-chip back to Remix (was briefly
    Coherent in v0.91.0). On-hardware a 4-chip Coherent run computed segment 0
    fine (~39s, 293W) but aborted (SIGABRT) during multi-board MESH TEARDOWN —
    `RiscFirmwareInitializer::teardown` timed out waiting for an ethernet core
    ("Device 0: Timed out ... active ethernet core 29-25 ... Try resetting the
    board"), the QB2's known-fragile cross-board fabric. Coherent chains
    segments by opening/closing the 4-chip mesh, so it exercises that fabric;
    Remix (independent 1x1 mesh per chip) does not. A default generation mode
    must not crash on the target hardware, so Remix is the default again;
    Coherent remains one dropdown-pick away (works when the board is healthy).
    Follow-up: make the coherent teardown resilient to the ethernet timeout
    (reset-and-retry) before promoting it to default. No wiring change — the
    v0.90.0 selector is unaffected.

