tt-local-generator (0.74.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * feat(pills): per-artgen-type Direction pills.
    - Each artgen medium (palette / verse / ansi / landscape / codeart /
      freeform) now shows its OWN curated chip banks in the Direction zone
      instead of the generic photo/video pills it inherited before (or no
      pills at all) — palette gets Mood/Era/Source/Harmony, verse gets
      Form/Tone/Voice, ansi gets Scene/Subject/Look, landscape gets
      Biome/Light/Style, codeart gets Structure, freeform gets Spark.
    - Every artgen type ALSO gets a shared cross-type "Feeling" mood bank
      (`for: [artgen]` in `config/prompt_chips.yaml`), deduped against any
      type-specific category of the same name
      (`chip_config.load_chips_for_artgen`).
    - New 🎲 Surprise chip: a category can mark one chip `surprise: true`
      (no `text:` needed) to apply a random pill from that category's own
      pool of non-surprise chips at click time (`chip_config.surprise_pool`,
      `ChipEntry.surprise`); unlike a normal add-chip it never hides itself,
      so it can be re-tapped for another random pick.
    - `ModifierPills(kind, artgen=True)` routes to the new
      `load_chips_for_artgen_kind` seam instead of the native
      `load_chips_for_kind`; `RoleZonePanel` now keys an artgen medium's
      pills by the medium's own type (`medium.id`) rather than its generic
      output `kind`, so e.g. palette and landscape no longer share one
      bank.
    - Native image/video mediums are unaffected (still keyed by `kind`, same
      banks as before); `collect()` is untouched on every surface — the
